adjudication.rationale:
In the newly added network-exposed handler `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook secret is validated via a direct string inequality check:
```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```
This is not a constant-time comparison and may allow timing-based guessing of `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (string comparisons can short-circuit). The endpoint also performs no visible rate limiting/throttling before allowing a credential create/update primitive (`prisma.credential.update/create`), making online guessing more feasible. Both issues are directly observable from the diff.
